se, "matchLevel": "full", "matchedWords": ["oversight"], "value": "https://www.msn.com/en-us/money/companies/nearly-1-billion-of-doge-savings-vanish-<em>overnight</em>/ar-AA1D7swu"}}, "_tags": ["story", "author_Jacquie11", "story_43721985"], "author": "Jacquie11", "children": [43721986, 43722006, 43722263, 43723409], "created_at": "2025-04-17T20:39:56Z", "created_at_i": 1744922396, "num_comments": 3, "objectID": "43721985", "points": 35, "story_id": 43721985, "title": "Nearly $1B of DOGE 'savings' vanish overnight", "updated_at": "2025-08-14T22:03:30Z", "url": "https://www.msn.com/en-us/money/companies/nearly-1-billion-of-doge-savings-vanish-overnight/ar-AA1D7swu"}, {"_highlightResult": {"author": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "hikerell"}, "story_text": {"fullyHighlighted": false, "matchLevel": "full", "matchedWords": ["oversight"], "value": "This week, my Vercel account was suddenly disabled and all of my deployments and data were deleted.<p>I received no warning, no suspension notice, and no post-action explanation. When I emailed their support to ask what happened, they refused to give a reason and simply said they wouldn\u2019t restore the account or data.<p>I\u2019ve been a Vercel user for over two years and never had any issue until now. It\u2019s honestly shocking to lose everything <em>overnight</em> without a single email or warning.<p>I\u2019m now migrating all my projects to Cloudflare, but the experience has been incredibly frustrating. I just want to understand why this happened \u2014 and whether anyone else has faced a similar sudden ban.<p>Has anyone here managed to get a clear answer from Vercel in a situation like this?"}, "title": {"fullyHighlighted": false, "matchLevel": "full", "matchedWords": ["oversight"], "value": "Lost all my sites <em>overnight</em>: Vercel terminated my account without notice"}}, "_tags": ["story", "author_hikerell", "story_45539442", "ask_hn"], "author": "hikerell", "children": [45540142, 45540263, 45542152, 45544021, 45544091, 45544595, 45575903, 45609596], "created_at": "2025-10-10T14:22:46Z", "created_at_i": 1760106166, "num_comments": 22, "objectID": "45539442", "points": 26, "story_id": 45539442, "story_text": "This week, my Vercel account was suddenly disabled and all of my deployments and data were deleted.<p>I received no warning, no suspension notice, and no post-action explanation. When I emailed their support to ask what happened, they refused to give a reason and simply said they wouldn\u2019t restore the account or data.<p>I\u2019ve been a Vercel user for over two years and never had any issue until now. It\u2019s honestly shocking to lose everything overnight without a single email or warning.<p>I\u2019m now migrating all my projects to Cloudflare, but the experience has been incredibly frustrating. I just want to understand why this happened \u2014 and whether anyone else has faced a similar sudden ban.<p>Has anyone here managed to get a clear answer from Vercel in a situation like this?", "title": "Lost all my sites overnight: Vercel terminated my account without notice", "updated_at": "2026-03-05T22:49:33Z"}, {"_highlightResult": {"author": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "vadumo"}, "story_text": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "Two days ago I had a working company. $1M ARR, 100k users, a product people actually pay for and depend on. Right now it's dead in the water and I'm locked out of all of it, because Google decided to suspend my entire account.<p>Someone got hold of one of my API keys and ran up charges on Google's AI services that I never touched. $4,200 hit my card for usage that wasn't mine. Fine, happens I paid the bill. But Google suspended my whole project. Everything lived in there. The backend, and every single customer photo, over a million of them.<p>So now my users open the app and nothing loads. I can't fix it because I can't even get into the console anymore, they took that away too.<p>I've spent two days appealing, paying for support just to reach a real human, getting &quot;escalated,&quot; and mostly sitting in an automated queue while my business bleeds. No real answer. No timeline. Nothing.<p>I trusted Google Cloud to hold my customers' data and run my company. Two days of downtime over a charge I didn't make, and all I can do is wait and hope someone over there decides to flip it back on. If you're building anything real, think hard before you put all of it somewhere that can be switched off like this. I'm moving everything I can to AWS.<p>If anyone at Google sees this, I've got my project ID and case numbers ready. If anyone have any contact that could help, I would appreciate"}, "title": {"fullyHighlighted": false, "matchLevel": "full", "matchedWords": ["oversight"], "value": "Google killed my $1M ARR startup <em>overnight</em>"}}, "_tags": ["story", "author_vadumo", "story_48396596", "ask_hn"], "author": "vadumo", "children": [48397356, 48405256, 48405914, 48406286, 48409040, 48409491, 48415470, 48422449, 48422785, 48430658, 48432999, 48433610, 48433806, 48437969, 48445402, 48450027], "created_at": "2026-06-04T10:26:15Z", "created_at_i": 1780568775, "num_comments": 16, "objectID": "48396596", "points": 25, "story_id": 48396596, "story_text": "Two days ago I had a working company. $1M ARR, 100k users, a product people actually pay for and depend on. Right now it&#x27;s dead in the water and I&#x27;m locked out of all of it, because Google decided to suspend my entire account.<p>Someone got hold of one of my API keys and ran up charges on Google&#x27;s AI services that I never touched. $4,200 hit my card for usage that wasn&#x27;t mine. Fine, happens I paid the bill. But Google suspended my whole project. Everything lived in there. The backend, and every single customer photo, over a million of them.<p>So now my users open the app and nothing loads. I can&#x27;t fix it because I can&#x27;t even get into the console anymore, they took that away too.<p>I&#x27;ve spent two days appealing, paying for support just to reach a real human, getting &quot;escalated,&quot; and mostly sitting in an automated queue while my business bleeds. No real answer. No timeline. Nothing.<p>I trusted Google Cloud to hold my customers&#x27; data and run my company. Two days of downtime over a charge I didn&#x27;t make, and all I can do is wait and hope someone over there decides to flip it back on. If you&#x27;re building anything real, think hard before you put all of it somewhere that can be switched off like this. I&#x27;m moving everything I can to AWS.<p>If anyone at Google sees this, I&#x27;ve got my project ID and case numbers ready. If anyone have any contact that could help, I would appreciate", "title": "Google killed my $1M ARR startup overnight", "updated_at": "2026-10-20T22:42:01Z"}, {"_highlightResult": {"author": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "tmcz26"}, "title": {"fullyHighlighted": false, "matchLevel": "full", "matchedWords": ["oversight"], "value": "Donald Trump says US is 'going to run' Venezuela after <em>overnight</em> strikes"}, "url": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/jan/03/caracas-explosions-venezuela-maduro-latest-news-updates-live"}}, "_tags": ["story", "author_tmcz26", "story_46479039"], "author": "tmcz26", "children": [46479350, 46479628, 46480273, 46480673, 46480726], "created_at": "2026-01-03T17:12:10Z", "created_at_i": 1767460330, "num_comments": 10, "objectID": "46479039", "points": 24, "story_id": 46479039, "title": "Donald Trump says US is 'going to run' Venezuela after overnight strikes", "updated_at": "2026-03-05T23:18:47Z", "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/jan/03/caracas-explosions-venezuela-maduro-latest-news-updates-live"}], "hitsPerPage": 40, "nbHits": 49, "nbPages": 2, "page": 0, "params": "query=oversight&tags=story&hitsPerPage=40&numericFilters=created_at_i%3E1735689600%2Cpoints%3